# TypeScript

Write all application code in TypeScript (`.ts` / `.tsx`). Do not add new `.js` or `.jsx` source files.

Use strict typing. Prefer explicit props and return types on exported functions. Avoid `any`; use `unknown` and narrow, or a precise type.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
export function formatPrice(value) {
  return "$" + value;
}

// ✅ GOOD
export function formatPrice(value: number): string {
  return new Intl.NumberFormat("en-US", {
    style: "currency",
    currency: "USD",
  }).format(value);
}
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
export default function ProductCard(props: any) {
  return <article>{props.title}</article>;
}

// ✅ GOOD
type ProductCardProps = {
  title: string;
};

export default function ProductCard({ title }: ProductCardProps) {
  return <article className="text-sm">{title}</article>;
}
```

- Import from `@/` (`src/*`) instead of long relative paths when crossing folders.
- Colocate types next to the module that uses them; export only when shared.
- Keep `strict` TypeScript; do not weaken `tsconfig.json` to silence errors.
